# Single-page app fallback: unknown paths serve the entry point rather than a
# 404, so a refresh or a deep link lands in the app.
#
# This lives in public/ (and so is copied into the publish directory) rather
# than only in netlify.toml, because a `netlify deploy --dir=...` upload carries
# the publish directory alone — the repo's netlify.toml is not consulted. Real
# files are matched before this rule, so it never shadows an asset.
/*  /index.html  200
